Give each illegal option pair one repair

Three options carry a glow form that needs the button effect, and the
two builds answer the same illegal pair with two values. The style
demotes the glow mouse-over to the thick coloured form and the glow
default button indicator to the tint. Both demotions sit inside the
block that CONFIG_DIALOG excludes. The dialog answers the first pair
with the Plastik mouse-over and the second by promoting the button
effect to Shadowed. A file that holds a glow with no button effect
therefore renders one way and shows another.

The focus repair holds a second fault. The reader forces every focus
except Glow to Line once the round rises above extra. The next repair
answers a missing button effect by turning a glow focus into the full
one. The second repair rebuilds the pair that the first forbids, so one
state reaches the style with two focus values.

Answer each illegal pair with one repair, and run the repairs in both
builds. Gather the three glow demotions under the button effect test.
Place the round repair after them, so it sees the focus that the button
effect leaves. A file that holds legal pairs reads exactly as it read
before.

The change sits on the branch work/config-io of the local tree, as commit 13 of 18.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/common/config_file.cpp b/qt6/common/config_file.cpp
index 39b1bc69..8f1b5e29 100644
--- a/qt6/common/config_file.cpp
+++ b/qt6/common/config_file.cpp
@@ -1128,22 +1128,29 @@ void qtcCheckConfig(Options *opts)
         opts->colorMenubarMouseOver=true;
 */
 
-#ifndef CONFIG_DIALOG
-    if(MO_GLOW==opts->coloredMouseOver && EFFECT_NONE==opts->buttonEffect)
-        opts->coloredMouseOver=MO_COLORED_THICK;
+    /* The three glow values need the button effect. One repair answers each
+       illegal pair, and both builds run it, so the dialog shows the value
+       that the style uses. */
+    if(EFFECT_NONE==opts->buttonEffect)
+    {
+        if(MO_GLOW==opts->coloredMouseOver)
+            opts->coloredMouseOver=MO_COLORED_THICK;
 
-    if(IND_GLOW==opts->defBtnIndicator && EFFECT_NONE==opts->buttonEffect)
-        opts->defBtnIndicator=IND_TINT;
+        if(IND_GLOW==opts->defBtnIndicator)
+            opts->defBtnIndicator=IND_TINT;
+
+        if(FOCUS_GLOW==opts->focus)
+            opts->focus=FOCUS_FULL;
+    }
 
+    /* A round above extra carries the glow focus alone. This repair runs
+       after the button effect repair, which can clear the glow. */
     if(opts->round>ROUND_EXTRA && FOCUS_GLOW!=opts->focus)
         opts->focus=FOCUS_LINE;
 
+#ifndef CONFIG_DIALOG
     if(EFFECT_NONE==opts->buttonEffect)
-    {
         opts->etchEntry=false;
-        if(FOCUS_GLOW==opts->focus)
-            opts->focus=FOCUS_FULL;
-    }
 
 //     if(opts->squareScrollViews)
 //         opts->highlightScrollViews=false;
